.Dd November 13, 2026
.Dt PATINA-KEYRING 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm patina-keyring
.Nd the Patina desktop's keyring password prompt
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Nm
.Fl h | V
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
asks for a keyring's password when logging in couldn't unlock it.
The keyring itself is
.Xr gnome-keyring-daemon 1 ,
which stores the passwords and tokens apps keep through the Secret Service and
is normally unlocked at login with your login password.
It asks only when that can't happen: after an automatic login or a fingerprint
login, when the keyring has another password than your login one, or when an
app creates a new keyring.
The daemon doesn't draw the dialog; it calls a prompter on the session bus,
and
.Nm
is that prompter, in place of GNOME's.
.Xr patina-compositor 1
keeps it running in the session.
.Pp
The dialog opens in the middle of the screen: a password, a new password
with a second box to repeat it in, or a question with two buttons, and the
daemon's tick box (unlock automatically whenever you're logged in) where it
asks for one.
Enter goes on, Escape or Cancel refuses.
A wrong password is asked for again.
.Pp
Only one prompter can have the bus names, so
.Nm
stops with an error where there already is one, as GNOME's
.Xr gcr-prompter 1 .
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h , -help
Print a short usage message.
.It Fl V , -version
Print the version.
.It Fl -ask Ar options
The dialog itself, which the prompter starts for each request; it answers on
standard output, so it isn't useful by hand.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev PATINA_SKIN
The skin to wear, as the bar sets it; otherwise the bar's config's.
.It Ev PATINA_KEYRING_DIALOG
A program to run in place of the dialog, with the same options, for tests
with no screen.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr gnome-keyring-daemon 1 ,
.Xr patina-compositor 1 ,
.Xr patina-polkit 1 ,
.Xr patina-desktop 7
